README for rootlesskit

Rootlesskit is a replacement for fakeroot which have the advantage 
of using the kernel, so it catches statically linked commands.

REQUIREMENTS

1. Kernel must have CONFIG_USER_NS defined to use namespaces

PRE/POST-INSTALL

1. Configure /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid for each userid that wants 
   to run as root. See https://access.redhat.com/articles/5946151
   or https://rootlesscontaine.rs/getting-started for example.

